<title>GERMANY: Deutsche Bahn approves Hamburg-Berlin Transrapid.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Bahn approves Hamburg-Berlin Transrapid.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The supervisory board of Deutsche Bahn AG has approved a controversial plan to build a Transrapid magnetic-levitation high-speed rail line between Hamburg and Berlin, chairman Heinz Duerr said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The plan was drawn up by private sector developers and the federal government as well as the Deutsche Bahn itself. A final decision will be made after another feasibility study due to be completed by June 1998, Duerr said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
